# SITE-V1 design and product constraints

- Implement the public projection; never turn visual/reference text into facts.
- Every repository artifact and public product is English, including site copy
  and the Software Development CV. Direct interaction with Andrés remains
  Spanish and does not change this file language.
- Surveda is the selected-work anchor only to the extent represented by the
  public-content projection.
- Use generic part-time/remote availability wording; no precise capacity figure
  unless a later projection deliberately contains it.
- Use `Software Developer` for the public Manas role unless a later projection
  explicitly changes it.
- Preserve one continuous page, normal scrolling and semantic order: Home,
  Experience, Background, Working together, Contact. CV is a utility, not a
  narrative station.
- R1 succeeds without moving cable. R2 may add deterministic S0–S3 behavior and
  three reversible anchors. R3 hardens production and final CV.
- The cable never carries unique information, blocks controls or consumes mobile
  reading width. Reduced motion keeps full understanding.
- Protect the editorial visual system and avoid generic developer-portfolio
  tropes. Treat reference PNG copy as non-authoritative.
